{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"[Download the cleaned March 2026 expense sheet (CSV)](/tmp/vellery-yfr30bic/work/march-2026-expenses.csv)\n\nThe CSV contains **18 expenses** in their original order. I removed the second copies of the March 2 office chairs and March 4 printer paper entries. I kept both `212.40` team lunches because they occurred on March 5 and March 25.\n\n**Date changes**\n\n| Expense | Original | Cleaned |\n|---|---|---|\n| Printer paper | `03/04/2026` | `2026-03-04` |\n| Team lunch | `March 5 2026` | `2026-03-05` |\n| Zoom subscription | `3/9/26` | `2026-03-09` |\n| Train tickets | `10/03/2026` | `2026-03-10` |\n| Monitor | `Mar 13` | `2026-03-13` |\n| Client dinner | `18/03/2026` | `2026-03-18` |\n| USB-C cables | `3/24/2026` | `2026-03-24` |\n\n**Category changes**\n\n| Expense | Original | Cleaned |\n|---|---|---|\n| Printer paper | `office supplies` | `Office Supplies` |\n| Taxi to client | `travel` | `Travel` |\n| Figma seats | `software` | `Software` |\n| Desk lamp | `furniture` | `Furniture` |\n| Pens | `Office supplies` | `Office Supplies` |\n\n**Amount changes**\n\n- Removed the dollar sign from all 15 retained amounts that had one.\n- Changed office chairs from `$1,240.00` to `1240.00`, removing the thousands separator.\n- Added decimal places to printer paper (`48.5` → `48.50`), Zoom subscription (`149` → `149.00`), and desk lamp (`$64` → `64.00`).\n\n**Uncertainty:** The sheet mixed month-first and day-first dates and omitted the year for `Mar 13`. Your instruction that every expense occurred in March 2026 resolved each case."}}
